   "text": "Fill inward0.00"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": "solid-cutaway-control",
   "text": "See inside"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-hint",
   "text": "Drag the prism to rotate · colored rays are samples of the extension on every ray."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-equation",
   "text": "x = ρu → F(x) = ρ B(u) + (1−ρ)r, ρ = 1 − fill"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-status",
   "text": "The dashed inner prism is not filled yet. Extend each boundary value inward along a ray; keep its original endpoint fixed."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "What am I looking at?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Here P is a rectangle or a solid triangular prism, hence a ball. Every point other than its center lies on a unique ray from the center to a boundary point u. Thus P is homeomorphic to Cone(∂P), with the original boundary as the base."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "B is the map already prescribed on ∂P. The target disk is our contractible allowed region. Its straight-line contraction to r gives F(ρu) = ρB(u) + (1−ρ)r. At ρ = 1 we recover B(u) exactly; at ρ = 0 every ray gives r. That is agreement and extension."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The slider reveals a fixed extension. It never changes an earlier boundary value. The same idea works for any contractible allowed region, using its contraction in place of straight lines."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Carrier proof · pp. 21–22 · Cones · Hatcher, Chapter 0"
  }
